+# Scientific v2 to v3 observer repair
+
+The sealed v2 diagnosis binds source manifest c937462c776f48ef3ce84d428ede3f3d5ccc4837c4874d54bd8961638a74bbc4 and external release9fe8f9dbac65aeb5ced77d83b3934dd7ee831a1563ddb24decfcef4749ee1e5f. The physical receipt records `RuntimeError: Owned live RSS observation missing`; the supervisor then sent owned SIGKILL and recorded exit−9. Session closure, direct-child reap and unresolved_cleanup=false are recorded. No RSS/wall/output cap breach is recorded, and MONITOR_FAILURE is absent. The exact task responsible was not logged; transient DataLoader exit after full VALID is consistent with the metadata, not proven attribution. No quality, state or stdout/stderr log was read.
+
+V2 reread task state after a status read and accepted missing VmRSS only for Z. A Linux task may release its mm before Z is visible. V3 uses one strict `/proc/PID/stat` text snapshot for RSS pages and identity. Valid R/S with RSS0 is included using that measured value; malformed or mismatched records fail. RSS field24 (index21 after comm) is multiplied by runtime page size. Missing tasks are omitted. Changed owned groups remain visible to the unchanged strict group guard. These are approximate sampled RSS observations.
+
+Only the existing supervisor `members_of_session` function changes, with two small sampler helpers added. Every other supervisor function, including main, process_identity, held_identity, kill_owned, cleanup, custody, active/spent locks and waitid/WNOWAIT, is AST-identical to v2. All executable code outside supervise.py is byte-identical except local source-check/regression code, which performs no numerical or process work. worker.py, common.py, data_adapter.py, model/config/dependencies/data/runtime authorities, all20 native files, sampling, AdamW, bf16/TF32, batch1024, accumulation8,12workers,20epochs, three scratchseeds and native scoring/strict first-tie selection are unchanged.
+
+Cap values and allocator policy remain v2:70GiB allocated,80GiB reserved,64GiB sampled sessionRSS,2GiB output and14400s per fit, with expandable_segments:True before Torch. The execution namespace and disabled proposed argv now use scientific v3. PLAN adds only failure provenance and sampler disclosure besides the namespace/observer protocol description. No existing scientific field or adaptation changes.
+
+The future root release candidate remains disabled with null authorization and exact-source/review/dependency placeholders. No execution root, client, launch, server operation, signal, donor, retry, resume, new resource-only fit or qualification ladder is supplied. Root separately reviews and consciously admits any future fresh queue when capacity is available. Original v1/v2 sources, failures, output directories and spent records are untouched. Copied failure metadata contains no predictive values and has consistent v2 source/release/physical identities. There is no closure ambiguity requiring invented qualification.
+
+sampler_regression.py extracts only the actual sampler helpers into a synthetic stdlib environment. It accepts R/RSS0,S/RSS0,S/positiveRSS,Z/RSS0; rejects negative RSS, mismatched PID, truncated fields and invalid page size; checks one stat read per listed task, disappearance, session filtering and changed group visibility. The checks read no live proc, create no process and send no signal. static_check.py rehashes the exact v2 source, compares all scientific/cap fields, verifies14 repair-input pins and verifies byte-identical failure metadata. These checks do not establish proc lifecycle execution, scientific feasibility or quality.
+
+V2_TO_V3.diff includes every changed inherited payload and every new payload available before this provenance/diff pair was generated. The provenance and manifest bind the diff and all remaining payloads without self-reference. Preserved earlier provenance and repair files are historical v1/v2 documents.
